COMPILATION OF: E49A2

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49A2

   1 a 0000 E49A2:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P1] the inverted compare under the BARE member
   4 a 0006      spelling: [C253]/[C258] fold `name' and `rec.name' to ONE
   5 a 0006      cell, and [C318]'s corroboration (E46K3, golden/e48p2retire)
   6 a 0006      proved spelling-invariance for a VARYING member in TEST; the
   7 a 0006      FIXED spelling in a compare has NEVER been sampled bare -- my
   8 a 0006      str_side admits only the qualified form (orig <> m.name). */
   9 c 0006   dcl
  10 c 0006     1 rec,
  11 c 0006       2 name char(3),
  12 c 0006       2 nxt fixed bin(15);
  13 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  14 c 0006   if name = 'AB' then k = 1;
  15 c 001D   put list('K=', k);
  16 c 003F   stop;
  17 a 0042 end E49A2;

CODE SIZE = 0042
DATA AREA = 000B
FREE SYMS = 3879
END  COMPILATION
